  "bull_bear_summary": {
    "bull_case": {
      "price_target_range": "$290-$325",
      "key_arguments": [
        "AI-driven content gain: 2nm ramp + vertical memory (HBM4) = content-per-wafer at all-time high; LRCX is the 'digital blacksmith' of the AI era",
        "Structural WFE growth: Management forecasts WFE $135B in CY2026 (up from $110B in CY2025), driven by DRAM + leading-edge foundry/logic for AI",
        "Market share gains at TSMC and in China foundry/logic segment",
        "Leadership across key inflection points: gate-all-around transistors (GAA), high-bandwidth memory (HBM4), advanced packaging - unique end-to-end tool presence",
        "Revenue trajectory: Management sees $25-28B by FY2028 (from $16.2B in FY2024), ~15-20% CAGR",
        "Record margins: Gross margin 49.7-50.6%, operating margin 34-35% in recent quarters, exceeding guidance",
        "14 consecutive earnings beats; avg trailing 4Q surprise +5.89%",
        "Onshoring/reshoring trends (CHIPS Act) create additional equipment demand",
        "Broad analyst upgrade cycle: Wells Fargo, Goldman Sachs, RBC, Cantor, Citi all bullish"
      ]
    },
    "bear_case": {
      "price_target_range": "$163-$204",
      "key_arguments": [
        "Memory cyclicality: Heavy reliance on DRAM/NAND manufacturers exposes LRCX to deep cyclical downturns",
        "China export restriction risk: Intensifying geopolitical pressures and export controls threaten significant China revenue (~30% of total)",
        "Valuation stretched: ~45x forward P/E on FY2026E demands sustained high growth execution",
        "NAND spending recovery uncertainty: While DRAM/HBM strong, NAND capex recovery timing remains unclear",
        "Insider selling: 8 insider trades in past 6 months, all sales",
        "Morgan Stanley (Shane Brett) remains Equal Weight — most conservative major bank despite triple PT raise",
        "Wide EPS estimate dispersion: B.Riley $4.63 vs consensus $5.35 for FY2026 suggests low visibility",
        "Stock up ~187% in one year from 52w low; macro risk (hawkish yields) could compress multiples"
      ]
    }
  },

